\ Interpreter-free AOT of a recursive combinator that calls its quotation
\ parameter (`over call`, effect unknown) and then self-recurses inside an `if`
\ arm -- the `(any-loop)` / `(all-loop)` shape from `#any` / `#all`. The self
\ call is reached after the dynamic `call` has collapsed the abstract stack to a
\ row, so it compiles to ordinary recursion; the codegen must not leave a
\ dangling loop frame. Exercised with both a plain predicate and a curry-closure
\ predicate.
any-loop: ( iter quot -- ? ) [
  over #next?
  dup option:some? [
    option:some> over call
    [ 2drop t ] [ any-loop ] if
  ] [ drop 2drop f ] if
] ;
my-any: ( seq quot -- ? ) [ swap >iterator swap any-loop ] ;

all-loop: ( iter quot -- ? ) [
  over #next?
  dup option:some? [
    option:some> over call
    [ all-loop ] [ 2drop f ] if
  ] [ drop 2drop t ] if
] ;
my-all: ( seq quot -- ? ) [ swap >iterator swap all-loop ] ;

{ 1 2 3 } [ 2 > ] my-any .
{ 1 2 3 } [ 5 > ] my-any .
{ 1 2 3 } 2 [ = ] curry my-any .
{ 1 2 3 } [ 0 > ] my-all .
{ 1 2 3 } [ 2 > ] my-all .
